**Rule.** The patient share on a Dental PPO Plans line reprocessed after a denial for the new waiting period that followed a change to a plan covering its service class (a reprocessed new-plan-wait line) follows the person and the other coverage:
(a) for a person receiving the pediatric essential-health-benefit treatment on a line from an in-network practice, the patient share is first limited to the pediatric out-of-pocket room (the pediatric out-of-pocket maximum for one child less the person's pediatric out-of-pocket postings net of reversals for the benefit year) and then reduced by any primary payment recorded on the line; the plan payment on such a line is the allowance less that limited share, so the line that crosses the pediatric out-of-pocket maximum pays the allowance minus the cost sharing still remaining, and a later line pays the full allowance;
(b) for any other line on which a primary payment above 0.00 is recorded, the patient share is reduced by that primary payment;
(c) otherwise the patient share is not adjusted;
and the patient share is never below zero.

**Figures.** Pediatric treatment: individual exchange enrollment, date of service before the person's 19th birthday (19 on every plan). One-child pediatric out-of-pocket maximum: 425.00 on Value 1000 and Plus 1500; 0.00 on the other plans. In-network practice: PPO or Premier in-network.

**Questions.**
*Pediatric member on Value 1000, in network, net pediatric postings 425.00 for the year?* No room remains; the patient share is 0.00 and the line pays the full allowance.
*Adult member, primary payment 18.60, share before this rule 40.15?* 40.15 less 18.60, which is 21.55.
*Adult member with no primary payment?* The share is not adjusted.
